cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CorpusPrep: corpus preparation for linguists"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adesokan
    given-names: Tosin
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-08-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adesokantosin2000-beep/corpusprep"
abstract: >-
  CorpusPrep prepares source texts for corpus analysis: the stage before
  AntConc or WordSmith Tools, both of which assume a clean corpus. Every line
  of a document is labelled before anything is removed, so the researcher
  decides what constitutes the corpus, and an accompanying log records how
  that decision was made. Detection never deletes, and every rule reports the
  evidence it acted on.

  Handles Project Gutenberg apparatus, mass-digitisation boilerplate, front
  and back matter, chapter and act segmentation, page furniture in scanned
  text, footnotes, hyphenation broken across line breaks, and paragraph
  reflow of hard-wrapped sources. Imports TXT, DOCX, EPUB and HTML. Runs as a
  Python package or as a single-file web application requiring no upload.
keywords:
  - corpus linguistics
  - text preprocessing
  - digital humanities
  - reproducibility
  - optical character recognition
  - text normalisation
